This example demonstrates 3D irreversible Marigo continuum surface damage with
a Peerlings implicit-gradient (Helmholtz) nonlocal energy filter on a closed
curved TRI6 spherical membrane in simple shear using `IBFESurfaceMethod`
(`examples/IBFE/explicit/ex14`).

Model helper (`IBFESurfaceDamage.h`):
Implements two-way elastic softening `(1 - d_eff)` for two-dimensional
in-plane Barthes-Biesel neo-Hookean (`BARTHES_BIESEL_NEO_HOOKEAN`) and Skalak
(`SKALAK`) thin-sheet energies on covariant surface tangents `G_0` and `G_t`
while keeping isotropic cortical prestress `T_0` undegraded. The model freezes
damage accumulation on folded elements (`Js_nod <= 0`), uses a read-only
explicit damage multiplier during RK2 substeps, commits damage once per
accepted time step, solves `(M_0 + l_d^2 K_0) Y_bar = M_0 Y` on the reference
surface via PETSc `MATAIJ`/`KSPCG`/`PCJACOBI` without altering libMesh
EquationSystems schemas, and gathers sorted slot keys collectively across MPI
ranks during SAMRAI restart serialization (`putToDatabase` / `getFromDatabase`).

Discretization note:
`example.cpp` builds a closed `320`-element `TRI6` spherical shell
(`R = 1.0`, `2` icosahedral subdivisions) in C++. `IBFESurfaceMethod` selects
`QGAUSS` / `FIFTH` quadrature automatically for second-order `TRI6` elements,
and `input3d` sets `IB_delta_fcn = "IB_4"`, `IB_point_density = 1.5`,
`use_consistent_mass_matrix = TRUE`, and `MAX_LEVELS = 1`.
